Z||000000||87FieroGT||10-27-2000||05:11 PM||||I had to replace my naster cylinder because it went bad.  I replaced the slave while I was at it.  When I first got the car I replaced the line with one from the factory so everything is new now. The slave and master are both Wagner products. The problem is that I can't seem to get the hydraulic pressure that is needed to release the clutch. It seems like air is getting into the system somehow. Is there supposed to be a rubber O-ring around the end of the clutch lines where they connect to the cylinders? If anyone here has worked with these products before I need your input to help me out. And before anyone suggests it YES I have looked at past posts about this problem. If anyone could help me I would greatly appreciate it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-27-2000||06:33 PM||||You must still have air in the system somewhere.<BR>No, there are no 'O' rings in it.<BR>||||reg||1
